  "version": "0.5.4-beta.3",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.5.4-beta.2`\n\n### Features\n\n- turn off timestamps in the plain-text log to keep output lines bare, file logs in folders by separating the name template with / (up to 5 deep, with year, month and day variables) and have the log list and cleanup look inside them and remove folders left empty, and tick sessions on the Terminal Logs page, one, a shift-click range or all shown, to delete them together ([e2b12e5b](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/e2b12e5b32c1a3d0c2b85ed908e654c264366b00))\n- connect as usual when a session's log cannot start and say so instead of failing the connection, and open a tab's newest log from its menu with View Logs, matched by the logs the tab wrote since tTerm started or, for a restored SSH tab, by its id and connection since tab ids are reused across runs ([e9710afc](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/e9710afcab5f705cdb6c5677f20cd16b6bf9d732))\n- browse logged sessions on a Terminal Logs page opened from Settings > Logs, replay a raw log in a read-only terminal with play, seek, speed, idle skipping and search, read the plain-text log, export a session as an asciicast recording, show it in its folder or delete it, and save a terminal's text with its scrollback from the terminal menu ([3923bd2b](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/3923bd2b7927223c2fcc0f7c4eeb629a54452e7f))\n- log sessions per connection (always, never or follow settings) or start and stop logging a tab from its menu with a mark on recording tabs, stop logging keyboard input unless turned on, clean up old logs by age or total size touching only files tTerm wrote, and build the plain-text log from the screen so it keeps each line as it finally appeared, notes full-screen programs instead of their frames and keeps what a cleared screen showed ([f28f8585](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/f28f8585edeaa23a838a4a8fe015bbd48ce5c2dd))\n\n### UI and usability\n\n- explain what unlimited scrollback really means: history grows up to 10 million lines and is only freed by clearing, memory per line grows with window width, all tabs share one interface process that may crash and lose every tab's scrollback past the system limit, and session logging is the way to keep output long term ([e5d0ab90](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/e5d0ab90c81719e9bb9863614ba15e161e0f670a))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.5.4-beta.2...v0.5.4-beta.3](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.5.4-beta.2...v0.5.4-beta.3)",
